# TypeScript/React Style Guide

- **Types first**: export shared interfaces/types from `src/types.ts`.
- **Explicit props**: annotate component props; avoid `any`.
- **State**: prefer context hooks from `src/context/**` over prop drilling.
- **Naming**: Components `PascalCase`, hooks `useX`, variables use full words.
- **Control flow**: use early returns; handle errors first.
- **Effects**: keep effects minimal; specify dependency arrays accurately.
- **Formatting**: match existing style; wrap long lines instead of one-liners.
- **Dead code**: remove unused imports/variables; fix linter warnings.
- **Composition**: leverage `components/ui/**` primitives for consistency.
- **Comments**: document non-obvious "why" above code; avoid inline noise.

